   "condition": "--cpus-per-task=1; Cpus_allowed_list 1; nproc 1; sched_getaffinity [1]; torch threads 1; jax default_backend cpu",
   "cores_cpu": 0.342,
   "decode_bar_fps": 4294.0,
   "host": "node2339.oscar.ccv.brown.edu",
   "job": "6409963",
   "mixed_default_batch": 64,
   "mixed_default_fps": 1469.1,
   "official_jitted_fps": 613.4,
   "paired_verdict": "USABLE -- baseline legs 101,598 and 105,684 f/s (spread 1.040), the baseline reproduces its known 115,166 f/s to 0.90x, load 0.92 per node core",
   "qualifiers": [
    "BELOW_G4"
   ],
   "s_cpu": 2.395,
   "superseded": "an earlier take on node2352 under --cpus-per-task=4 read S_cpu 3.810. It is NOT the number: torch.set_num_threads(1) binds torch and says nothing about jax, whose CPU backend has its own pool, so the reference could use four cores while ours used one. The two takes also differ by node, so the drop from 3.810 to 2.395 is not cleanly attributable to the core budget -- what is attributable is that only the second was taken under the condition the ladder is defined at",
   "tier": "CPU_FASTER"
  },
  "performance_record_gpu": {
   "R": 100.96,
   "backend_class": "R",
   "batch_scales": "425x (fps(4096)/fps(1)) against the 20x bar, measured on the sibling gpu2106 run of the same code, job 6397699; the R run drew B=256 and 4096 only, so its own record carries no B=1 cell",
   "card": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090",
   "condition": "same card, same job; the official timed from $SCR/venvs/se7-craftax-gpu with jax.default_backend() == 'gpu' and devices ['cuda:0'] ASSERTED before timing, jitted, warm, 6.72 s of compile excluded; ours timed from $SCR/venvs/se7-craftax on the same allocation",
   "cores": 21.82,
   "decode_bar_fps": 4323.3,
   "host": "gpu2109.oscar.ccv.brown.edu",
   "job": "6410052",
   "mixed_batch": 4096,
   "mixed_fps": 94343.9,
   "official_jitted_fps": 934.5,
   "size": 10,
   "tier": "GPU_FASTER",
   "why_not_no_reference": "$SCR/venvs/se7-craftax is a jax[cpu] build, so jax.default_backend() is 'cpu' inside a GPU job whatever JAX_PLATFORMS says; job 6409535 would have timed the 'same-card reference' on the CPU and was cancelled before it ran. W1's jax[cuda12] venv was reused rather than a second one built, and it carries no torch, so the two interpreters share one allocation"
  },
